            "review_title": "Review at Lotus Lounge",
            "review_text": "thom_hdz\nParis, France3 contributions\n0\nAbsolutely unacceptable management\nAug 2026 • Couples\nFrankly mind-blowing experience at the Vietnam Airlines Lounge 1 at Ho Chi Minh City airport.\n\nOur Vietnam Airlines flight was initially scheduled to take off at 10:50 PM. It was finally delayed by more than two hours, with a new departure scheduled around 1:00 a.m.\n\nWe arrive at the lounge around 7:30 p.m., thinking we can wait for our flight there in good conditions.\n\nAnd there, right at the entrance, we are told very calmly that the maximum duration is 3 hours and that we will therefore have to LEAVE the lounge around 10:30 p.m.\n\nExcuse me?\n\nVietnam Airlines delays our flight by more than two hours, forces us to spend a good part of the night at the airport, and its lounge's response is to ask us to leave because we will have exceeded the 3-hour limit?\n\nYou have to have some nerve.\n\nI can perfectly understand that a time limit is applied in normal times. On the other hand, applying it without the slightest flexibility when the overage is directly linked to the airline's own flight delay shows a rather spectacular lack of common sense and consideration for passengers.\n\nAnd that is precisely where the service becomes particularly disappointing: no understanding of the situation, no solution proposed, no exception considered. Just: \"3 hours maximum\".\n\nWhen you present yourself as a lounge offering a premium service, serving a few dishes, providing Wi-Fi, and making armchairs available is not enough. The true level of service is measured precisely when a problem arises.\n\nSubjecting passengers to more than a two-hour delay and then explaining to them that they will have to leave the lounge in the middle of their wait because their time is up is quite surreal.\n\nVietnam Airlines should seriously review the way this rule is applied in the event of delays to its own flights.\n\nAn extremely disappointing experience and a level of service very far from what one is entitled to expect from an airline like Vietnam Airlines.\nRead more\nTranslated from French\nShow original\nWritten August 31, 2026",
